WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:01.789
Next question.

00:00:01.789 --> 00:00:09.330
Hey, David, will Corona virus finally be the
catalyst we need for people to do mass call

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.269
outs of work?

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:17.180
Large scale strikes, coordinated mortgage
and rent defaults and all of those other protest

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.860
and activism techniques that you've been talking
about?

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:20.950
Beautiful question.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.899
I have talked about those techniques before.

00:00:22.899 --> 00:00:27.410
I've said many, many times signing petitions
online.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:28.650
OK.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.279
Calling your elected officials great.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:40.780
But that in order to really change the system
from the point of view of an activist, you

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:47.030
may have to be willing to participate in some
other types of protest.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:51.370
And this includes, as the question asks.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:55.920
Large scale strikes, mass call outs, strategic
defaults, etc.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:01.730
The question of whether a corona virus will
cause that to happen really comes down to

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:04.089
one element.

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:07.580
And that's how long does this all last.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:13.650
And the reason I say that is that for a lot
of people, the twelve hundred dollars stimulus

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.690
is not going to be enough.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:22.350
People on unemployment will be able to sort
of remain afloat treading water.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:28.420
Assuming that this doesn't last that much
longer than what the models suggest.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.800
And most people.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.610
And this is a feature of the system, not a
bug.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:39.121
From the purposes of corporate, the corporatocracy,
as soon as things start to open back up, people

00:01:39.121 --> 00:01:41.200
are going to have to go back to work.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.460
OK, this is how the system is designed.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:50.189
So I often say to you, one of the impediments
to mass rallies to change the system is that

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:54.560
the system makes it so that people have to
keep going to work.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.950
People would potentially lose health insurance
if they bail on their job.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:08.220
The system is insulated from being changed
by how it sort of controls the people that

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.769
are working within the system.

00:02:09.769 --> 00:02:15.529
So in the same way right now, a lot of people
are staying home and people understand, particularly

00:02:15.529 --> 00:02:19.439
on the left, that you've got to stay home
to stop the spread of the virus.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:22.750
So right now, you're not going to see those
mass rallies because people are doing the

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.950
right thing once things start to open up.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:30.060
The people who have been staying home are
also likely to understand the importance of

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:34.919
getting back to work, to feed their families
and to get caught up with rent or mortgages

00:02:34.919 --> 00:02:36.480
or whatever the case may be.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:42.180
So the system has a way of perpetuating itself
by always making it difficult and inconvenient

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:46.349
and very risky to actually go out and do that
type of protesting.

00:02:46.349 --> 00:02:51.639
Now, as far as, you know, formal rent strikes,
for example, a coordinated rent strike would

00:02:51.639 --> 00:02:57.470
be large swaths of people say we are not paying
rent on this day or we are not paying our

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:01.940
mortgages on this day, a strategic mortgage
default.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:08.250
There is no doubt that if it comes down to
you, pay your rent or you buy food or you

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.019
buy medication.

00:03:10.019 --> 00:03:15.180
I would expect that rent comes after food
and medication.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.949
Of course, every situation is different.

00:03:16.949 --> 00:03:17.949
Depends.

00:03:17.949 --> 00:03:18.949
What is the medication I get?

00:03:18.949 --> 00:03:21.599
But generally speaking, that is probably the
case.

00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:26.629
But remember, evictions have been slowed down
or stopped in many areas.

00:03:26.629 --> 00:03:30.400
There are places that have done rent and mortgage
deferrals.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.250
Now, importantly, that's not forgiveness.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:36.840
A lot of people, I hope, are our understanding,
but I fear that some people are not.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:42.689
When you talk about a rent deferral for three
months, that means you don't pay April 1,

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:44.589
May 1, June 1 rent.

00:03:44.589 --> 00:03:47.089
But on July 1, you owe all four months.

00:03:47.089 --> 00:03:48.230
Now, maybe it'll be phased.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:52.530
Then maybe you've got to make up half of each
of the deferred months per month through the

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.379
end of the year or something like that.

00:03:54.379 --> 00:04:00.239
Still, a lot of it is up in the air, but those
deferrals are only deferrals.

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:02.129
It is not forgiveness.

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:05.069
And that is going to be a problem on the tail
end for a lot of people.

00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:09.189
If you needed to defer one months of rent,
are we likely to imagine that you're going

00:04:09.189 --> 00:04:12.219
to be able to afford four months of rent on
July 1st?

00:04:12.219 --> 00:04:14.750
It doesn't strike me that way.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:20.130
But again, when it comes to the system, I
don't know that you will see as many rent

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:26.370
and strategic mortgage defaults because evictions
and foreclosures have been slowed down or

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.460
stopped in many parts of the country.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:34.120
And again, it's the system perpetuating itself,
the system protecting itself.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.900
This gets me back to the beginning.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.940
Ultimately, this will depend on how long this
goes.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:44.490
It's early, but there are starting to be some
improving numbers in many U.S. states and

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.840
in many countries around the world.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:52.780
Social distancing must remain, but it is not
crazy to think that at some point in the not

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:57.780
too distant future, I allow the doctors to
tell us when I'm not even going to speculate.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:04.250
Some elements of the economy may be ready
to be open back up, including with young workers,

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.400
people who test positive for antibodies, meaning
they've already built an immunity to the Corona

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.260
virus, et cetera.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:14.770
And that one factor, how long this goes and
how successfully we stop the spread is going

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:20.800
to be primarily the determining factor as
to how motivated people are to look at large

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.180
scale strikes, mass call outs, etc..

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:29.750
My prediction is anybody who can get back
to work whenever it is, mostly people are

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:31.830
going to be glad to do that.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:37.990
And given the choice between starting to earn
money immediately or going in striking most

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:38.990
people.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.650
I'm not saying this is good or bad, I'm just
saying this is.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.590
Most people are going to choose to get back
to work and to start earning money.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:46.520
That's my my prediction.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.780
Let me know if you disagree.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:52.250
Let me know what you think should happen with
regard to mass rallies and call outs.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:55.180
We've got a fantastic bonus show for you today.

